{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d41ca70-372d-4892-8970-7a61f415a27a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"An inscribed angle has its vertex on a circle. Its two sides meet the circle at A and B.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Inscribed angle theorem"},{"op":"figure","id":"circle_fig","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.8,3.8],"y":[-3.8,3.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"circle","id":"rim","center":[0,0],"r":3},{"kind":"point","id":"a","at":[-2.598076211,-1.5],"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"b","at":[2.598076211,-1.5],"label":"B"},{"kind":"point","id":"p","at":[0,3],"label":"P"},{"kind":"segment","id":"pa","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"a"}},{"kind":"segment","id":"pb","from":{"at":"p"},"to":{"at":"b"}},{"kind":"angle","id":"inscribed","at":{"at":"p"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.16,"label":"θ"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d41ca70-372d-4892-8970-7a61f415a27a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The intercepted arc is the arc from A to B that avoids P. The central angle measures that same arc.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"central_marks","on":"circle_fig","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"o","at":[0,0],"label":"O"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"o"},"to":{"at":"a"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"o"},"to":{"at":"b"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"arc","center":{"at":"o"},"r":3,"start":210,"end":330,"label":"120°"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"o"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.2,"label":"120°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"central_eq","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\angle AOB=120^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d41ca70-372d-4892-8970-7a61f415a27a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The inscribed angle equals half the central angle subtending the same arc. Here, half of 120 degrees is 60 degrees.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"theorem","anchor":{"el":"central_eq","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\theta=\\frac12\\angle AOB"},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"theorem","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\theta=\\frac12(120^\\circ)=60^\\circ"},{"op":"figure","id":"answer_mark","on":"circle_fig","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0,1.65],"text":"60°","size":"normal"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"8d41ca70-372d-4892-8970-7a61f415a27a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Move the vertex along the opposite arc: the angle stays 60 degrees because it still intercepts the same arc AB.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"second_vertex","on":"circle_fig","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"q","at":[-3,0],"label":"Q"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"q"},"to":{"at":"a"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"q"},"to":{"at":"b"},"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"q"},"from":{"at":"a"},"to":{"at":"b"},"r":0.18,"label":"60°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"same_arc","anchor":{"el":"example","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\angle AQB=\\angle APB=60^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the central angle subtending an arc is 80°, what is an inscribed angle intercepting that arc?","expected_gist":"40°: half the central angle."}}}
